<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xliff xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:2.0" xmlns:swi18n="https://step-wise.com/ns/i18n" version="2.1" srcLang="en" trgLang="nl">
	<file id="catalog">
		<group id="practice">
			<group id="applyPythagoreanTheoremGeneral">
				<unit id="mainProblem">
					<segment>
						<source>Given the triangle below, determine the unknown side <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</source>
						<target swi18n:sourceContentFingerprint="2519c97319e8cf18" swi18n:sourceStructureFingerprint="8c52ffd8f6d33b16">Gegeven is de onderstaande driehoek. Vind de onbekende zijde <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</target>
					</segment>
				</unit>
				<group id="step1">
					<unit id="problem">
						<segment>
							<source>Through the Pythagorean therom, set up an equation linking the three sides of the triangle. Use the values <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>, <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> and <ph id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</source>
							<target swi18n:sourceContentFingerprint="7a18528a34620bf1" swi18n:sourceStructureFingerprint="29f4bdc3e3cb616a">Stel via de stelling van Pythagoras een vergelijking op voor de zijden van de driehoek. Gebruik de waarden <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>, <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> en <ph id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</target>
						</segment>
					</unit>
					<unit id="solution">
						<segment>
							<source>We have the two legs <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> and <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> and the hypothenuse <ph id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>. The Pythagorean theorem now directly states that <ph id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:block-math"/></source>
							<target swi18n:sourceContentFingerprint="fd8d4c783a32ef98" swi18n:sourceStructureFingerprint="c349a010fef3c387">We hebben hier rechte zijden <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> en <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> en schuine zijde <ph id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>. De stelling van Pythagoras zegt nu direct dat <ph id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:block-math"/></target>
						</segment>
					</unit>
				</group>
				<group id="step2">
					<unit id="problem">
						<segment>
							<source>Solve these equation first for <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</source>
							<target swi18n:sourceContentFingerprint="055852c1124cc78f" swi18n:sourceStructureFingerprint="8c52ffd8f6d33b16">Los deze vergelijking eerst op voor <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</target>
						</segment>
					</unit>
					<unit id="solution">
						<segment>
							<source>We can directly find that <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:block-math"/> This can then still be simplified to <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:block-math"/></source>
							<target swi18n:sourceContentFingerprint="6982828469f8ecb2" swi18n:sourceStructureFingerprint="b44bdd9ade835acd">We kunnen direct vinden dat <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:block-math"/> Dit kan vervolgens nog vereenvoudigd worden tot <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:block-math"/></target>
						</segment>
					</unit>
				</group>
				<group id="step3">
					<unit id="problem">
						<segment>
							<source>Determine based on <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> the value of <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</source>
							<target swi18n:sourceContentFingerprint="d84ca52930fd373c" swi18n:sourceStructureFingerprint="98f3255e641e5524">Bepaal vanuit <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> de waarde van <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</target>
						</segment>
					</unit>
					<unit id="solution">
						<segment>
							<source>We take the square root of both sides of the equation. This gives us <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:block-math"/> Note that, since we know that the requested distance is positive, we do not need to add a <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> here. <pc id="x1" type="other" subType="swi18n:condition" swi18n:variable="$condition1"><pc id="x2" type="other" subType="swi18n:condition-true">Optionally, the above result can still be simplified to <ph id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:block-math"/></pc><pc id="x3" type="other" subType="swi18n:condition-false">The above result cannot be simplified further.</pc></pc></source>
							<target swi18n:sourceContentFingerprint="07fc5997554a060b" swi18n:sourceStructureFingerprint="3908a0a697b8d786">We nemen van beide kanten van de vergelijking de wortel. Zo vinden we <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:block-math"/> Merk op dat, omdat we weten dat de gevraagde afstand positief is, we hier geen <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> bij hoeven te plaatsen. <pc id="x1" type="other" subType="swi18n:condition" swi18n:variable="$condition1"><pc id="x2" type="other" subType="swi18n:condition-true">Eventueel kan het bovenstaande nog vereenvoudigd worden tot <ph id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:block-math"/></pc><pc id="x3" type="other" subType="swi18n:condition-false">Het bovenstaande kan niet nog verder vereenvoudigd worden.</pc></pc></target>
						</segment>
					</unit>
				</group>
			</group>
		</group>
	</file>
</xliff>
